Feature addition: bullet damage persistence — penetrating shots for high-damage weapons.

This commit modifies 5 files (+325/-13 lines), spanning 2 core game loop, 1 game entities, 1 tests.
This feature extends the Geometry Wars 3D codebase with new functionality. The implementation follows the project's established patterns and maintains compatibility with both single-player and multiplayer code paths where applicable.

Key files: src/core/CollisionSystem.ts, src/core/GameInstance.ts, src/entities/Bullet.ts, ...13-bullet-damage-persistence.regression.test.ts, ...2-13-bullet-damage-system-damage-persistence.md.

Geometry Wars 3D supports 8 distinct map surfaces: sphere, torus, peanut, pill, cube, Möbius strip, sphere-tunnel (bevel), and a flat surface. Each surface requires specialized UV handling, tangent frame computation, and collision detection. New features must work correctly across all surfaces in both single-player (via GameLoop.ts) and multiplayer (via network-main.ts) code paths. SP and MP code paths are entirely separate — changes to one do not automatically apply to the other.
